WEBVTT

00:09.320 --> 00:12.240
I will wipe you out.

00:15.530 --> 00:18.410
Fly high, make it

00:18.410 --> 00:21.660
Get to the new world that I seek

00:21.870 --> 00:28.170
Someday with my little wings

00:28.340 --> 00:34.420
Don't look back to the sorrow I left behind

00:34.720 --> 00:40.640
Here's my real intention I hide

00:41.260 --> 00:47.400
I wish you were here, and so just right by my side

00:47.690 --> 00:53.780
Need to be strong enough to swallow my pride

00:53.990 --> 00:59.660
I have been looking for my own style

00:59.660 --> 01:07.170
Don't give it up, here comes the life

01:10.090 --> 01:12.840
Be alive, take it

01:12.840 --> 01:16.090
Promise to find, yes I will

01:16.340 --> 01:22.560
Shining wings filled with wishes

01:22.850 --> 01:25.600
Fly high, make it

01:25.600 --> 01:29.100
Get to the new world that I seek

01:29.150 --> 01:35.570
Someday, so I believe

01:49.250 --> 01:50.250
Yes.

01:51.000 --> 01:51.750
Ah.

01:52.000 --> 01:53.130
I'm here.

01:54.750 --> 01:59.760
Hey, wait! You're showing the door to your best friend who came to visit you so late at night?

01:59.760 --> 02:01.510
I don't have a best friend. Go home!

02:01.510 --> 02:02.510
What?

02:02.970 --> 02:06.930
Open up! This is the FBI! You have the right to remain silent.

02:06.930 --> 02:12.110
Ah, stop it. I got it. I got it. So give me five minutes. I'm going to clean up my room!

02:13.020 --> 02:15.320
Are you trying to hide your ecchi books?

02:15.320 --> 02:17.820
It's not like that. Anyway, wait outside...

02:24.700 --> 02:26.330
You're a manga artist?

02:26.330 --> 02:29.960
Yeah. I'm already an active professional.

02:29.960 --> 02:31.420
I see.

02:31.880 --> 02:36.000
I thought it was strange for you to skip school all the time, even though you're a diligent person.

02:36.000 --> 02:37.710
Don't tell anyone.

02:37.710 --> 02:40.470
Okay. However, there's a condition.

02:40.470 --> 02:41.380
Condition?

02:49.020 --> 02:52.100
I don't have the right to tell him my feelings.

02:52.100 --> 02:53.270
Onii-chan

02:54.610 --> 02:57.780
Ah, is this Kei? I need to talk to you about something.

03:01.030 --> 03:02.410
It hurts.

03:02.410 --> 03:06.410
Is it that amusing to make fun of people?

03:06.660 --> 03:09.120
It's all thanks to you saying something weird.

03:09.120 --> 03:13.750
When I scout for an actress, I have a higher chance to succeed by doing that.

03:14.040 --> 03:15.960
What about an actress?

03:19.630 --> 03:22.720
When will this become interesting?

03:22.720 --> 03:24.720
It will be like this throughout the whole thing.

03:25.220 --> 03:28.310
How long do I need to watch this?

03:28.310 --> 03:30.430
About two more hours.

03:31.270 --> 03:35.980
Don't show me boring stuff. Because I don't have time.

03:36.270 --> 03:37.940
Which parts were boring?

03:38.360 --> 03:42.950
Which parts...? The actors were bad, the story was cliche.

03:42.950 --> 03:46.490
I thought it was interesting at the beginning, but it became boring as it went along.

03:46.780 --> 03:50.500
Why did you think it was interesting at the beginning then?

03:50.500 --> 03:54.500
Hm, that's because... it looked beautiful.

03:54.920 --> 03:59.500
The acting was bad, but they, somehow, appeared lively.

03:59.500 --> 04:02.300
Eh, you have an eye for it.

04:02.760 --> 04:07.470
The director and scenarist were my senpai in the film research club, but I was the cameraman.

04:07.800 --> 04:09.100
It's a nice film, isn't it?

04:10.430 --> 04:14.980
And it seems Kyosuke wants to make a new film.

04:14.980 --> 04:16.230
With you as the leading actress.

04:16.230 --> 04:17.150
Eh?

04:18.820 --> 04:22.110
Kei-chan, can you participate in my film?

04:24.450 --> 04:27.280
You're the only character.

04:27.280 --> 04:30.200
You just need to come along with me whenever you're available.

04:30.200 --> 04:32.500
I will then follow you around with my camera.

04:32.500 --> 04:36.080
But I'm an amateur when it comes to acting.

04:36.080 --> 04:38.710
It's okay. There's no script.

04:39.040 --> 04:43.090
I will just record the way you're living and your feelings just as they are.

04:43.090 --> 04:45.090
My... feelings?

04:45.380 --> 04:47.260
Is it something like a documentary?

04:47.590 --> 04:51.060
Nah, it's neither a documentary nor a drama.

04:51.060 --> 04:52.770
I'm not going to assume anything beforehand.

04:52.770 --> 04:54.980
I will polish the film from the material I get.

04:55.230 --> 04:56.520
Hm...

04:56.520 --> 04:57.270
What?

04:57.520 --> 05:00.360
Can you do it without a vision to start with?

05:00.360 --> 05:03.940
I don't want to be bound by the vision I created at the beginning.

05:03.940 --> 05:07.780
With only an ideal that's hit-or-miss, you won't be able to produce something good.

05:07.780 --> 05:12.290
Even if I produce something good, it will be meaningless if it's not a film I want to make.

05:12.700 --> 05:15.580
Let me give you a word of advice from a professional's point of view.

05:15.580 --> 05:18.670
It's not that easy to make something.

05:18.670 --> 05:21.920
Do you think it's easy to just make it at will?

05:21.920 --> 05:24.710
It's even more difficult than those professions with fixed boundaries.

05:24.710 --> 05:27.630
Professionals have to struggle with those boundaries.

05:27.630 --> 05:30.680
It's a different meaning from freedom gained without fighting.

05:31.260 --> 05:34.060
The area I want to fight in is different from yours!

05:34.060 --> 05:37.940
I want to make my film without being bound by the evaluation of the audience and judges!

05:37.940 --> 05:41.060
Do you only consider the readers when you draw?

05:41.440 --> 05:44.650
I'm also trying to draw something that I want to draw!

05:44.650 --> 05:47.900
It won't work if I only consider the readers, will it?

05:47.900 --> 05:51.280
Do you shoot your films without considering the audience?

05:51.280 --> 05:57.790
Whether it's just one scene or one cut, I want to make a film that shakes the souls of those who see it.

05:58.540 --> 06:03.500
For that sake, it won't work if that moment doesn't shake my own soul.

06:04.800 --> 06:06.760
If you say so, try and do it.

06:06.760 --> 06:08.630
Yeah, I will do it.

06:09.260 --> 06:12.140
Hey, don't decide on your own.

06:12.140 --> 06:15.390
I didn't say that I would participate in the film.

06:16.350 --> 06:17.390
Huh?

06:17.680 --> 06:19.810
Well, take your time and think about it.

06:19.810 --> 06:22.480
It's pointless to wait for me, so please give up.

06:22.900 --> 06:25.230
Well then, I will look forward to your favorable reply.

06:25.230 --> 06:27.240
Listen to what others say!

06:29.030 --> 06:32.070
I wonder what he's planning to do with the movie he's making of me.

06:32.070 --> 06:35.240
If you plan to appear in his film, be careful.

06:35.240 --> 06:38.710
That guy is a womanizer.

06:38.710 --> 06:41.790
Hm, you're worrying about me, eh?

06:41.790 --> 06:43.250
Idiot.

06:46.590 --> 06:47.590
Onii-chan.

06:49.090 --> 06:53.340
Does Miyamura-senpai always come to your room?

06:54.180 --> 06:56.060
She's only been there two to three times.

06:56.060 --> 06:56.760
Really?

06:57.180 --> 06:58.810
Hey, Onii-chan.

06:59.230 --> 07:02.770
Do you, perhaps, think I'm... annoying?

07:02.980 --> 07:03.650
Huh?

07:03.940 --> 07:07.940
I come to wake you up in the morning, and I nag you to go to school.

07:08.740 --> 07:12.110
Onii-chan, don't you think I'm annoying?

07:12.410 --> 07:16.410
What are you saying all of a sudden? That's not true.

07:16.950 --> 07:20.830
Whenever I talk to you about something serious, you're unwilling to listen.

07:20.830 --> 07:23.040
You weren't like that before.

07:23.040 --> 07:26.420
It's different from before. I'm not a kid anymore.

07:26.790 --> 07:31.590
Onii-chan, you matured too soon.

07:34.050 --> 07:35.930
Incoming Mail

07:34.050 --> 07:35.930
Chihiro

07:34.840 --> 07:35.930
It's Chihiro.

07:36.640 --> 07:38.470
She's talking about Renji-kun again.

07:38.810 --> 07:41.270
Chihiro was able to make a friend?

07:41.270 --> 07:44.270
Yeah. Lately, she looks happy.

07:44.270 --> 07:46.400
Could it be... her boyfriend?

07:46.400 --> 07:51.860
Hm, I wouldn't say so, but it looks like it will be soon, from the way it's going.

07:52.150 --> 07:54.240
I see. That's good.

07:55.950 --> 07:56.490
Yeah.

07:58.200 --> 08:00.080
Hey, Onii-chan.

08:00.080 --> 08:02.830
Our basketball club has a match on Sunday.

08:02.830 --> 08:04.000
Will you come and watch?

08:04.000 --> 08:05.210
Match?

08:05.210 --> 08:07.960
That match, I'll win for sure.

08:08.290 --> 08:12.630
If I win, I will have something important to tell you.

08:12.630 --> 08:15.180
Something important? What is it?

08:15.180 --> 08:18.220
Right now, it's a secret. I will tell you by then.

08:18.550 --> 08:19.390
Hey!

08:19.390 --> 08:21.470
I'll win for sure!

08:25.020 --> 08:27.650
Have you read Chihiro's novel?

08:27.650 --> 08:31.940
Yeah, it was quite amazing. How come Chihiro could write something like that?

08:32.400 --> 08:36.780
For Chihiro, writing down her words is the same as surviving.

08:37.160 --> 08:38.030
Surviving?

08:38.570 --> 08:41.080
She's conveying her image to another person.

08:41.080 --> 08:45.080
Herself in the past and the one reading it are two different beings.

08:45.750 --> 08:51.050
Chihiro uses her diary to connect her gradually disappearing self to the future.

08:51.800 --> 08:56.300
How accurately can she convey her own image to a different being?

08:57.010 --> 08:59.430
What she's doing is the same as a writer.

08:59.430 --> 09:03.640
Chihiro's writing skill is the same as a novelist's.

09:03.640 --> 09:07.560
That skill won't improve without a good memory, will it?

09:08.150 --> 09:10.520
It might be her natural talent.

09:10.860 --> 09:14.780
Even if you lose your memory, there might be something that permeates through your body.

09:15.110 --> 09:17.320
It could also be because she desperately wants to convey it.

09:17.320 --> 09:19.200
That's why such an ability resulted.

09:20.830 --> 09:24.660
Well, since you have already come this far, just pray that she will finish writing it.

09:24.910 --> 09:28.460
Himura-san, who on earth are you?

09:28.460 --> 09:29.830
What do you mean?

09:29.830 --> 09:32.300
Like what you do for a living.

09:32.300 --> 09:34.710
How come you're always at this church?

09:35.380 --> 09:38.220
I have been... waiting for someone.

09:38.220 --> 09:39.300
Waiting for someone?

09:39.970 --> 09:42.470
I'm not a pastor nor a counselor.

09:42.470 --> 09:46.060
But, to guide, I dare to give you advice.

09:46.640 --> 09:48.350
Don't get too involved with Chihiro.

09:52.440 --> 09:54.780
"The girl began to paint."

09:55.280 --> 09:57.740
"Books, musical instruments, pictures."

09:57.740 --> 10:03.280
"Among those things, it was the tool that's most likely to create a human."

10:04.910 --> 10:07.660
"But it didn't go well."

10:08.410 --> 10:10.000
"She got tired of it many times."

10:10.000 --> 10:11.830
"It didn't matter anyway, even if she got tired of it."

10:12.250 --> 10:16.670
"When the season changed, she had enough."

10:17.340 --> 10:19.430
"She finished the painting before long."

10:19.840 --> 10:24.600
"She found out that she was more suited for drawing realistic scenes."

10:25.310 --> 10:29.060
"As long as she was able to draw something that looked like it, it was fine."

10:29.060 --> 10:30.480
"Something that didn't exist there."

10:30.980 --> 10:34.190
"Drawing humans might be something hard to do."

10:34.520 --> 10:35.940
"That's what she thought."

10:38.820 --> 10:40.200
Let's take a break.

10:40.200 --> 10:41.030
Okay.

10:41.410 --> 10:44.030
Is there some place you're stuck?

10:44.030 --> 10:47.580
Yes. About the castle that the girl lives in...

10:47.580 --> 10:49.960
I can't come up with an image of the warehouses.

10:49.960 --> 10:51.250
Warehouse, eh?

10:51.670 --> 10:53.080
The warehouse for food.

10:53.540 --> 10:57.210
The warehouse that stores the stuff she needs for living.

10:57.210 --> 11:01.720
And the warehouse of books where she reads to gain knowledge.

11:01.720 --> 11:07.720
There are others as well, including the landscape of the island and the shapes of wild plants, I can't come up with.

11:08.140 --> 11:10.850
That means we need more data, eh?

11:10.850 --> 11:13.060
Only if there was a library.

11:13.060 --> 11:14.480
Yeah.

11:14.980 --> 11:18.440
The only library in Otowa is the one at school.

11:19.280 --> 11:20.570
Let's go and take a look.

11:20.570 --> 11:21.900
Where are we going?

11:22.160 --> 11:23.410
To school.

11:34.000 --> 11:37.380
And? What business do you have with me?

11:37.380 --> 11:41.130
I'm sorry for saying something boring to you the other day.

11:41.470 --> 11:44.260
Something boring? What was it?

11:45.640 --> 11:50.270
I have been hanging out with Hirono-senpai since we were children.

11:50.270 --> 11:52.230
Yeah, I know.

11:52.230 --> 11:56.440
When he was small, Hirono-senpai didn't have any friends.

11:56.440 --> 12:00.230
I couldn't stand watching Hirono-senpai, who was always alone.

12:00.230 --> 12:03.490
Because of that, I brought him to my home.

12:03.910 --> 12:07.490
You brought a boy back home all of a sudden?

12:07.490 --> 12:09.990
You are pretty bold.

12:10.240 --> 12:14.710
Is that your way of changing the subject?

12:14.710 --> 12:19.130
Serious subjects are hard to follow.

12:19.920 --> 12:23.670
I had a lot of shoujo manga in my room.

12:23.930 --> 12:27.930
That was the first form of entertainment that Hirono-senpai ever touched.

12:28.180 --> 12:30.930
Senpai was really absorbed by it.

12:31.850 --> 12:35.690
But I never thought that he would become a professional.

12:36.060 --> 12:39.480
Hirono-senpai's talent is amazing.

12:39.860 --> 12:41.780
I think...

12:42.820 --> 12:46.780
Just watching someone doing his best and thinking he's amazing is not good enough.

12:47.280 --> 12:51.740
Someone who's doing his best wouldn't accept someone who's doing nothing after all.

12:51.740 --> 12:54.540
At least, I don't think he would like her.

12:54.830 --> 12:57.960
I guess that's the reason you started playing basketball?

12:58.330 --> 13:03.590
You told me that I was showing my honesty in the wrong place, right?

13:04.090 --> 13:06.180
To Onii-chan, I...

13:11.390 --> 13:17.850
It's been like that since a long time ago, and it will be like that forever from now.

13:17.850 --> 13:20.190
My feelings will go on forever.

13:20.190 --> 13:22.530
Because my feelings, even up till now, have never stopped once.

13:24.070 --> 13:26.610
Even if you're telling me this...

13:27.860 --> 13:30.870
Just like that, you should just keep playing dumb.

13:34.290 --> 13:36.750
I will never lose to you.

13:38.870 --> 13:43.800
I will wipe you out from Onii-chan's heart.

13:46.800 --> 13:48.260
I am...

13:46.840 --> 13:48.010
I am —

13:48.090 --> 13:50.260
Going to disappear

13:48.260 --> 13:50.470
going to disappear

13:50.340 --> 13:51.550
from Hirono-kun's heart • • •

13:50.470 --> 13:51.550
from Hirono-kun's heart...

13:54.930 --> 13:58.940
Together, Onii-chan and I will start from there.

13:59.270 --> 14:01.400
He will then say farewell to you.

14:01.400 --> 14:03.610
And then, it will be over.

14:05.860 --> 14:07.360
I will end this.

14:09.660 --> 14:13.580
I'm going to disappear... I'm going to disappear again...

14:17.330 --> 14:21.040
Say, Mom. Is there anyone who has a spare uniform?

14:21.040 --> 14:22.790
Like someone who didn't get to graduate.

14:22.790 --> 14:25.300
My, is it torn somewhere?

14:25.300 --> 14:29.880
I'm not talking about mine. I'm wondering if there's any spare girls' uniform.

14:30.130 --> 14:33.180
I want you to ask around in cooking class.

14:33.180 --> 14:34.760
Would you mind?

14:34.760 --> 14:36.810
Ah. It's for Chihiro-chan, right?

14:37.220 --> 14:40.730
If it's used clothes, I can borrow from everyone, then there's no problem.

14:40.730 --> 14:41.520
Really?

14:41.520 --> 14:45.610
Now thinking about it, Kuze-san also has a uniform.

14:45.860 --> 14:48.900
I'm talking about a girl's uniform though.

14:49.150 --> 14:51.070
That's right. A girl's.

14:52.070 --> 14:54.830
Why does Kuze-san...

14:55.580 --> 14:57.330
Yeah, I do have one.

14:58.080 --> 14:59.540
Where did I put it?

14:59.540 --> 15:06.840
Erm, it's okay if you don't want to answer, but why do you have something like that?

15:06.840 --> 15:09.590
Oh my, you're a boy too.

15:09.590 --> 15:13.430
In other words, it's a souvenir, plus now when it feels like the relationship is lacking freshness,

15:13.430 --> 15:15.430
I'll let her wear it, then strip half of it away.

15:15.430 --> 15:20.180
Even though it sounds like a roundabout way, it's too easy to understand. Forget it.

15:20.180 --> 15:22.190
What are you two talking about?

15:22.190 --> 15:23.270
Ah.

15:23.270 --> 15:23.770
Ah?

15:24.150 --> 15:26.190
You're going to let Chihiro-chan wear it, eh?

15:26.190 --> 15:28.650
Please don't imagine something weird.

15:28.650 --> 15:31.490
Erm, what are you two talking about?

15:32.030 --> 15:35.120
I wonder if this size fits you. Want to give it a try?

15:35.120 --> 15:37.870
Size... Are you collecting them?

15:38.200 --> 15:38.990
A little.

15:39.790 --> 15:41.210
You're hopeless.

15:44.880 --> 15:51.880
Now thinking about it, why does my mom know that you have girls' uniforms?

15:52.220 --> 15:58.100
Ah. Because I think she's cute, so by all means, I wanted her to wear them.

15:58.100 --> 16:01.390
What on earth are you asking someone's wife to do?!

16:01.930 --> 16:04.810
Erm, do you have a moment?

16:04.810 --> 16:07.400
Ah, the size didn't fit you?

16:07.770 --> 16:14.910
The size fits me, but I think the type is not right...

16:14.910 --> 16:17.780
Kuze-san, this...

16:17.780 --> 16:21.290
When one talks about uniforms, this is what it means after all.

16:21.290 --> 16:23.410
You're really hopeless.

16:26.210 --> 16:29.040
Erm, I'm done changing.

16:31.510 --> 16:34.720
This is Otowa's school uniform, right?

16:34.720 --> 16:35.340
Yeah.

16:35.340 --> 16:38.510
It's the same as Onee-chan's, right?

16:38.510 --> 16:40.260
Yeah, that's right.

16:42.140 --> 16:43.310
How is it?

16:43.310 --> 16:45.980
It suits you really well, Chihiro.

16:46.350 --> 16:47.230
Okay.

16:47.520 --> 16:50.480
Let's wear that and go to school tomorrow.

16:51.860 --> 16:52.990
What's wrong?

16:52.990 --> 16:56.700
Erm... Can't we go now?

16:57.820 --> 16:58.450
Yeah.

17:02.450 --> 17:03.450
Incoming Mail

17:02.450 --> 17:03.450
Chihiro

17:03.450 --> 17:05.920
I like the cool Onee-chan

17:03.450 --> 17:05.920
I think you should be honest with yourself

17:06.290 --> 17:07.420
Chihiro...

17:07.420 --> 17:08.170
Thank you

17:08.170 --> 17:09.170
E-mail Sending• • •

17:13.670 --> 17:15.170
Jan.

17:15.170 --> 17:21.310
Today I used a lot of effort and made unagi no hitsumabushi.

17:21.310 --> 17:23.390
Eels killing time?

17:23.390 --> 17:27.650
That's right. After the day of the ox during midsummer, the eel has a lot of free time...

17:23.390 --> 17:25.390
The day of the ox is a calendar system that counts the days according to the twelve zodiacal signs.

17:25.390 --> 17:27.650
For 2007, that day was the 30th of July. It's a tradition in Japan to eat eels on that day.

17:27.650 --> 17:29.900
Who said it's eels killing time?!

17:27.650 --> 17:31.270
Miyako said "Unagi no Hitsumabushi",
while Hiro heard it as "Unagi no Himatsubushi".

17:31.900 --> 17:33.780
It's unagi no hi-tsu-ma-bu-shi.

17:35.400 --> 17:39.910
Say, Hirono-kun. Do you have work to do this weekend?

17:39.910 --> 17:40.410
Ah?

17:40.410 --> 17:43.120
Sunday, let's go somewhere to play.

17:43.410 --> 17:47.790
Between deadlines, I make sure to sleep as much as I can on holidays.

17:47.790 --> 17:49.630
I don't have the time to play.

17:50.580 --> 17:51.670
You liar.

17:52.670 --> 17:56.510
I know. The basketball club has a match, right?

17:56.720 --> 17:59.760
Oh. I didn't lie. I just forgot about it.

18:00.010 --> 18:02.260
Are you going after all, then?

18:02.260 --> 18:05.600
I didn't really promise to go.

18:05.600 --> 18:06.930
Really?

18:06.930 --> 18:07.600
Yeah.

18:08.100 --> 18:11.230
In that case, make a promise with me.

18:11.940 --> 18:14.610
Go out on a date with me on Sunday.

18:14.610 --> 18:17.950
Eh? Nah, I just said on holidays...

18:17.950 --> 18:18.820
You can't?

18:18.820 --> 18:19.820
Nah...

18:20.240 --> 18:22.320
Let's go. Together.

18:50.230 --> 18:51.810
Kei-chan!

18:51.810 --> 18:52.810
INFIRMARY

18:53.650 --> 18:57.530
Don't be so depressed. There will be another match, right?

18:57.990 --> 18:59.490
It's not that.

19:00.650 --> 19:02.280
It's not about that.

19:04.530 --> 19:09.290
I told you I would use my right hand if you shot without my permission again, didn't I?

19:09.290 --> 19:11.870
Yeah. You can hit me as much as you like.

19:12.540 --> 19:15.000
This is a moment that I can't find otherwise.

19:15.000 --> 19:18.170
If I let it go now, I won't be able to get it back again.

19:18.550 --> 19:21.340
"I won't be able to get it back again..."

19:21.340 --> 19:24.890
I want to catch irreplaceable moments like that.

19:24.890 --> 19:28.020
For the sake of that, I will do it no matter what.

19:28.310 --> 19:31.940
Even if you do it, everything will be over if you fail.

19:31.940 --> 19:33.520
It won't be over.

19:33.520 --> 19:35.980
As long as I don't give up, it won't be over.

19:35.980 --> 19:37.940
I will keep challenging it.

19:39.740 --> 19:40.530
How's Kei?

19:40.990 --> 19:43.530
Onii-chan, why?

19:43.530 --> 19:46.240
Well, I contacted him.

19:46.620 --> 19:47.740
Are you all right?

19:48.080 --> 19:51.080
It's dizziness caused by light anemia and dehydration.

19:51.080 --> 19:54.630
And it seems she hit and injured her knee when she fell.

19:54.880 --> 19:56.380
Onii-chan...

19:56.710 --> 19:58.880
You idiot.

20:01.380 --> 20:03.930
Geez, I said I'm fine.

20:03.930 --> 20:06.100
This is embarrassing. Let me down.

20:06.100 --> 20:08.470
Shut up. Be a good girl.

20:08.470 --> 20:10.220
Geez, you're always doing stupid things.

20:10.520 --> 20:13.480
What? You've been calling me an idiot since earlier.

20:13.480 --> 20:16.020
You're an idiot for pushing yourself until you collapsed.

20:16.020 --> 20:18.230
I just tripped a little.

20:18.230 --> 20:20.900
It's okay, be quiet. Don't force yourself.

20:20.900 --> 20:22.780
I'm not forcing myself.

20:22.780 --> 20:25.530
You're always overdoing it.

20:25.530 --> 20:28.080
Aren't you the same?

20:29.490 --> 20:31.580
It's fine for me.

20:31.950 --> 20:34.330
What's that?

20:37.500 --> 20:40.800
Onii-chan, you're wearing your good clothes.

20:40.800 --> 20:41.710
Eh?

20:41.710 --> 20:44.510
Have you been on a date with Miyamura-senpai?

20:44.510 --> 20:47.010
Ah, I stood her up.

20:47.390 --> 20:48.470
Is that okay?

20:48.470 --> 20:52.060
Stupid, I can't just leave you alone, can I?

20:53.640 --> 20:55.480
I have to apologize to her.

20:55.980 --> 20:58.270
Ah, this is bad. I dropped my cell phone.

20:59.480 --> 21:00.360
What?

21:00.610 --> 21:01.650
Nothing.

21:02.440 --> 21:06.740
By the way, didn't you say you had something to tell me after the match was over?

21:07.410 --> 21:09.410
It doesn't matter anymore.

21:13.330 --> 21:14.660
School...

21:14.660 --> 21:15.160
Eh?

21:20.380 --> 21:21.920
My heart is pounding.

21:21.920 --> 21:25.670
It's okay. If you walk as usual, nobody will notice.

21:26.130 --> 21:28.510
How do I walk usually?

21:32.060 --> 21:33.520
I can smell the books.

21:45.650 --> 21:46.900
Thank you.

21:48.160 --> 21:50.280
Thank you, Renji-kun.

22:04.380 --> 22:11.680
yumemiteta hitori

22:04.380 --> 22:11.680
I dreamed of being alone

22:12.930 --> 22:23.230
sora miage itsuka mabushii ta

22:12.930 --> 22:23.230
Looking up at the sky which once had dazzled me

22:23.480 --> 22:31.950
itami wo omoidasu no

22:23.480 --> 22:31.950
I remember my pain

22:32.030 --> 22:43.500
shiroi hane ni kaze wo fuke

22:32.030 --> 22:43.500
Blow wind, to the white feathers

22:43.790 --> 22:55.220
yureru kioku ni kagi wo toke

22:43.790 --> 22:55.220
Unlock the key to my wavering memories

22:55.310 --> 23:06.480
todoke hate made douka kanata he

22:55.310 --> 23:06.480
Please reach the other side, even if it means the very end

23:06.820 --> 23:15.370
egao anata ni modoru

23:06.820 --> 23:15.370
I will return the smile to your face

23:15.660 --> 23:18.200
ashita he

23:15.660 --> 23:18.200
Towards tomorrow

23:26.040 --> 23:27.380
NEW MAIL

23:26.040 --> 23:27.380
99 ITEMS

23:28.260 --> 23:33.050
What I want to reach you are not words, but myself.

23:33.050 --> 23:38.100
Next episode, ef - a tale of memories: I...

23:38.100 --> 23:41.020
Do you have memories you don't want to forget?
